  message: "Post-close bakeoff validation 2026-05-31 (via WI-kaziv on cohort #1 of broad-20260531-022124). Positive evidence: Go aliased package imports verified working on webtunnel (pt for goptlib correctly resolves to full package paths). Adjacent-but-not-direct: (a) Rust grouped-use + qualified call on non-std crates remains unresolved —  +  produces no calls edge in webassembly-component-tutorial. WI-vipur's scoped_path mode was wired with std as the implicit-import; non-std crates may be a follow-up gap. (b) JS constructor () and default-import () cases still unresolved, but these were not in WI-kujom's stated scope (which was aliased named imports + function call). dst_ref structured field confirmed visible on JS edges in {lang, module_path, name} form; not observed in this cohort's Go/C/Erlang/Rust/Swift edges (whether by design or because the construct didn't trigger is undetermined from this cohort alone). Full per-repo verdict: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/wi-kaziv-bakeoff-verdict-05312026.md. No actionable regression filed; the partial-positive signal is consistent with WI-mafik's claims at the polyglot-fixture level, but the prospector-corpus signal is weak due to cohort sampling. No status change."  # c9b7
